# Copy to deploy/.env (never commit it) and fill in. Read by docker compose and the Slider container.
# Full list and explanations: docs/self-hosting.md

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public host name; DNS must point at this server. Slider runs at https://${SLIDER_DOMAIN}.
SLIDER_DOMAIN=slider.example.com
# openssl rand -hex 24   (hex only: it ends up inside DATABASE_URL)
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Everything below is optional. Login, mail and sign-up can also be set up in the browser: after
# the first start, `docker compose logs slider` shows https://<SLIDER_DOMAIN>/einrichtung and a
# one-time "Setup token". Enter it there; once signed in, enter it again to become instance admin
# (signing in alone makes nobody admin). Values set here win and appear read-only on that page.

# Generated into the data volume on the first start when empty. Only set it to pin a value
# (openssl rand -base64 48; ≥ 32 characters; signs sessions, encrypts tokens and settings).
# SLIDER_SECRET=

# Encrypts files, comments, slide texts, deck titles and file names at rest. Set it here, outside
# the data volume, so backups of the volume don't carry it – and keep a second copy (password
# manager): without it the content is lost. Never change it. Empty: generated into the data volume
# (/data/data-key) on the first start. A new key only before the first start; once Slider ran,
# copy /data/data-key here instead (docs/self-hosting.md → Schlüssel sichern).
#   openssl rand -base64 32 | tr '+/' '-_' | tr -d '='
# SLIDER_DATA_KEY=

# Behind Cloudflare (orange cloud): trust its edge addresses so rate limits see the visitor.
# Current list: https://www.cloudflare.com/ips/ – leave empty without Cloudflare.
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=173.245.48.0/20 103.21.244.0/22 103.22.200.0/22 103.31.4.0/22 141.101.64.0/18 108.162.192.0/18 190.93.240.0/20 188.114.96.0/20 197.234.240.0/22 198.41.128.0/17 162.158.0.0/15 104.16.0.0/13 104.24.0.0/14 172.64.0.0/13 131.0.72.0/22 2400:cb00::/32 2606:4700::/32 2803:f800::/32 2405:b500::/32 2405:8100::/32 2a06:98c0::/29 2c0f:f248::/32

# ── Sign-up ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# open = anyone who can sign in (default; the first login creates the account)
# invite = only invited people · domains = anyone from SIGNUP_DOMAINS
# company = invited people and anyone at a domain an organisation is opened to
# SIGNUP=open
# SIGNUP_DOMAINS=firma.de,firma.com

# ── Privacy ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Delete accounts and decks nobody used for 18 months (reminder mails before, if mail is set up).
# On by default; also on the setup page (/einrichtung → Datenschutz).
# DELETE_UNUSED=false

# ── Plans ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your server, your rules: no limits by default. Set single ones if you want (0 = unlimited);
# SLIDER_DEMO=true turns on the hosted demo's free plan (5 people, 3 decks, one own
# organisation per account, 2 GB of storage per organisation).
# PLAN_FREE_MAX_MEMBERS=
# PLAN_FREE_MAX_DECKS=
# PLAN_FREE_MAX_STORAGE_BYTES=
# SLIDER_DEMO=false

# ── Login (or on the setup page) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Microsoft (Entra app registration; redirect URI https://<SLIDER_DOMAIN>/api/auth/microsoft/callback)
# MS_CLIENT_ID=
# MS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MS_TENANT=common

# Nextcloud of the organisation (optional; any Nextcloud works without it, see docs/self-hosting.md)
# NEXTCLOUD_URL=https://cloud.example.com

# Google login (redirect URI https://<SLIDER_DOMAIN>/api/auth/google/callback; docs/self-hosting.md),
# Google Drive comes with it (enable the Google Drive API and Google Picker API in the project).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# OIDC, e.g. Keycloak (redirect URI https://<SLIDER_DOMAIN>/api/auth/oidc/callback)
# OIDC_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com/realms/firma
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# OIDC_LABEL=Weiter mit Firmen-Login

# Invitations by e-mail (optional), e.g. Brevo: smtp://<login>:<smtp-key>@smtp-relay.brevo.com:587
# SMTP_URL=smtps://user:password@smtp.example.com:465
# MAIL_FROM=Slider <slider@example.com>

# Stock photos in the editor and for the AI (optional): the Access Key of an app at
# https://unsplash.com/oauth/applications (docs/self-hosting.md → "Fotos").
# UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Several apps on this server: use the shared Caddy of deploy/proxy instead of Slider's own
# (docs/self-hosting.md → "Proxy und Cloudflare").
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.shared-proxy.yml
# Only the server of the product website: serve apps/site at https://${WEBSITE_DOMAIN}/slider/
# through this Caddy as well (docker-compose.website.yml).
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.website.yml
# WEBSITE_DOMAIN=bertro.dev
# Its own checkout, written by .github/workflows/deploy-website.yml on every push to main
# (default /opt/slider-site).
# WEBSITE_DIR=/opt/slider-site
# Where its contact form (/slider/kontakt) is mailed – needs SMTP_URL and MAIL_FROM.
# CONTACT_EMAIL=slider@bertro.dev
SYNC_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=60000
SYNC_DEBOUNCE_MS=60000
